## 1. Method

Model risk is assessed on the two axes of the FDA credibility framework: the
influence of the agent's output on the decision, and the consequence of that
decision being wrong. The combination is read from an explicit matrix, after
which escalation rules are applied. No rule lowers a risk class.

Severity, probability and detectability for individual failure modes follow the
two-step method common to GAMP 5 and ICH Q9(R1): severity and probability give
a priority, which detectability then modifies, because a failure that cannot be
seen cannot be corrected.

